'''Familiars''' are small companions, usually generated by [[Items#Passive Collectibles|passive items]], that follow and assist Isaac. Effects of familiars include (but are not limited to) [[pickup]] generation, shooting familiars that fire their own tears at enemies, and ''orbitals'' that act as projectile shields and/or deal contact damage.

Many of these familiars (especially pickup generation and shooting familiars) follow behind Isaac. When Isaac picks up multiple of these following familiars, they form a line behind him from oldest to newest (with closest familiar behind Isaac being the oldest one picked up) rather than constantly overlapping one another on the same spot behind Isaac.
* {{dlc+|r}} In addition to being chronologically ordered, certain familiars on the line take priority over others in how close their position is to Isaac. There are the following priorities, in order:
*# {{I|King Baby}}, making it always the closest familiar to Isaac.
*# {{I|Incubus}}.
*# {{I|Milk!|r+}}.
*# {{I|Lil Portal|r+}}.
*# {{I|Lil Brimstone}} and {{I|Lil Monstro}}.
*# {{I|Censer}}, {{I|Dry Baby}}, {{I|Lil Abaddon}}, and {{I|Mongo Baby}}.
*# Most shooting familiars and some throwable familiars.
*# Most pickup generation familiars and "<code>[[Item Tags quest|quest item]]</code>" familiars such as {{I|Key Piece 1}}. {{I|Boiled Baby}} also takes this priority.
{{dlc-}}
Isaac cannot have more than 64 total familiars at once. This includes blue spiders and flies, familiar items such as {{I|Dry Baby}}, {{c|Tainted Eve|r}}'s blood clots, etc. Gaining more than this will result in familiars being destroyed, with blue spiders and flies being destroyed first.

